Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.32,0:00:04.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now the crowd law: on average,\Nenergy in equals energy out.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.00,0:00:09.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Three ways to impose it,\Nat settings of {\c&H7AAF1B&}eta{\c&HF7F4F2&} never seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.26,0:00:14.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One: during training, the crowd\Nloss, with its two juries.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.27,0:00:16.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Against a control run of equal length,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:16.82,0:00:21.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}the {\c&H00A1ED&}distribution distance{\c&HF7F4F2&} drops from\Ntwo point five to zero point seven.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.95,0:00:24.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The control itself gains nothing.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.13,0:00:28.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Two: after training,\Nreweight the generated crowd.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.77,0:00:32.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Where the model is worst,\Na poll of five hundred
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.14,0:00:35.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}shrinks to one person,\Nand the crowd gets worse.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.72,0:00:39.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Three: rescale every\Nsnapshot onto the budget.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.93,0:00:43.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Each snapshot now dissipates\Nthe same: a spike,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.08,0:00:45.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}under a thousandth of the true spread.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.92,0:00:51.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Yet the same {\c&H00A1ED&}distribution distance{\c&HF7F4F2&},\Nbuilt on spectra, improves: it is fooled.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.29,0:00:56.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Only the spread gives the spike away.\NThe crowd loss shows no spike.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.93,0:00:59.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}One training seed each,\Ninterpolation only,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.61,0:01:02.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}every model far above the noise floor.
